  "body": "In some situations `[SecureContext]` is implied through an object's exposure. Concretely, interfaces only exposed in Service Workers are per definition limited to secure contexts because Service Workers themselves are. Should we still specify `[SecureContext]` on such interfaces? It's clear, but redundant.\r\n\r\nThis came up in https://github.com/w3c/push-api/pull/284 for the `PushEvent` and `PushSubscriptionChangeEvent` interfaces.",
